L624:   Similar increases were found for the mature ribosomal species 18 s (1.18‐fold) and 28 s (1.16‐fold), in addition to the 45 s pre‐ribosomal rRNA (1.19‐fold) using qPCR ( Figure 
L625:  10 ). No changes were observed for 5.8 s (1.07‐fold,  P  = 0.722) or 5 s (1.06,  P  = 0.940) following the entire training intervention. Notably, for analyses of total RNA and ribosomal RNA, an additional time point were included in main analyses, i.e. in muscle biopsies sampled after introduction to training (3.5 weeks, 7 sessions), as early increases in total RNA seem to associate with long‐term chronic responses to training, making it a potential hallmark of muscle plasticity. 
